 class="cf-trigger " title="A custom COP formula can be pasted here to run the integration and optimization with a specific heat pump.">ƒ Use my own COP formula</button></div></div></div><details><summary style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-weight: 500; cursor: pointer;">More options</summary><div class="pa-opt-toggles" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 0.75rem;"><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox" checked=""><span>Show theoretical heat pumps (1)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Carnot and the best technology archetype, as reference points against the modelled machines.</span></span></label><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox"><span>Plot source-limited points (7)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">These cover only part of the demand up to the sink temperature, so they lie off the sink profile.</span></span></label><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox"><span>Plot demand-limited points (23)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">These cover the full demand but leave waste heat unused at the source temperature, so they lie off the source profile.</span></span></label></div></details></div><div class="pa-opt-chart" style="display: flex; min-width: 0px; overflow: hidden;"><div data-testid="chart">{"points":"232:a45f089d","maxQ":"Test@113","selected":[],"pinch":73,"mode":"net_load"}<button data-testid="chart-pick"></button></div></div></div></div></div></div>"`;

