ss="cf-trigger" title="The 2-temperature COP model (source out, sink out): the heat pump drawn, values can be tried and the COP is shown">COP model</button></div></div><div class="cf-trigger-block"><div class="cf-trigger-head"><label style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-weight: 500;">COP SOURCE</label><div class="chart-help-container inline"><button class="btn btn-sm chart-help-btn  " title="Show explanation"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-info" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4"></path><path d="M12 8h.01"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="cf-trigger-row"><button class="cf-trigger " title="A custom COP formula can be pasted here to run the integration and optimization with a specific heat pump.">ƒ Use my own COP formula</button></div></div></div><details><summary style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-weight: 500; cursor: pointer;">More options</summary><div class="pa-opt-toggles" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 0.75rem;"><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox" checked=""><span>Show theoretical heat pumps (1)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Carnot and the best technology archetype, as reference points against the modelled machines.</span></span></label><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox"><span>Plot source-limited points (7)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">These cover only part of the demand up to the sink temperature, so they lie off the sink profile.</span></span></label><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox"><span>Plot demand-limited points (23)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">These cover the full demand but leave waste heat unused at the source temperature, so they lie off the source profile.</span></span></label></div></details></div><div class="pa-opt-chart" style="display: flex; min-width: 0px; overflow: hidden;"><div data-testid="chart">{"points":"232:a45f089d","maxQ":"Test@113","selected":["Butane_1@89.5","Butane_1@95.5"],"pinch":73,"mode":"net_load"}<button data-testid="chart-pick"></button></div></div></div></div></div><div class="cf-backdrop" role="presentation"><div class="cf-modal hpv-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="COP model"><header class="cf-header"><h3>COP model</h3><button class="cf-close" aria-label="Close"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-x" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18"></path><path d="m6 6 12 12"></path></svg></button></header><div class="cf-body"><div class="hpv-morph"><button type="button" class="hpv-morph-end">Heat pump</button><input min="0" max="1" step="0.01" aria-label="From the heat pump to the COP model" aria-valuetext="Heat pump" type="range" value="0"><button type="button" class="hpv-morph-end">COP model</button></div><div class="hpv-toolbar"><span class="cf-muted">Temperatures on the shifted scale, as the optimization uses them (ΔTmin/2 = 5.0 K).</span></div><svg class="hpv-diagram" viewBox="0 0 1000 450" role="img" aria-label="Heat pump"><defs><marker id="hpv-a-src" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="12