OP model</button></div></div><div class="cf-trigger-block"><div class="cf-trigger-head"><label style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-weight: 500;">COP SOURCE</label><div class="chart-help-container inline"><button class="btn btn-sm chart-help-btn  " title="Show explanation"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-info" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M12 16v-4"></path><path d="M12 8h.01"></path></svg></button></div></div><div class="cf-trigger-row"><button class="cf-trigger " title="A custom COP formula can be pasted here to run the integration and optimization with a specific heat pump.">ƒ Use my own COP formula</button></div></div></div><details><summary style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-weight: 500; cursor: pointer;">More options</summary><div class="pa-opt-toggles" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 0.75rem;"><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox" checked=""><span>Show theoretical heat pumps (1)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Carnot and the best technology archetype, as reference points against the modelled machines.</span></span></label><label style="margin-top: 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgb(100, 116, 139); cursor: pointer;"><input style="margin-top: 0.15rem;" type="checkbox"><span>Plot source-limited points (7)<br><span style="font-size: 0.75rem;">These cover only part of the demand up to the sink temperature, so they lie off the sink profile.</span></span></label><label style="ma